This covers src/incident2chaos/data/corpus.csv, src/incident2chaos/data/blind_sample.csv,
src/incident2chaos/data/pilot_check.csv, src/incident2chaos/data/fault_classes.json, src/incident2chaos/data/triggers.json,
data/codebook.md and data/site_terms.md.

Attribution: Yogesh Ramaswamy (2026), corpus and codebook of “Which Real Cloud Failures Can Chaos Tools Inject? A Mapping Study of 437 Public Post-Incident Reports and Two Fault Catalogs”.

The reports themselves belong to their publishers and are not included. The corpus holds
only each report's link, its title and date as the publisher's index lists them,
labels, and short notes that paraphrase the report. A language model proposed every
label and wrote the notes of the 447 first-pass rows; the author checked the labels of
the 50 pilot rows and changed 10.
